@template dry
// ZW1 (writer), patch 0.92.3 item 26: crew comment when you wear dirty clothes. clothes.remark: yesterday's clothes
// (flag:clothes.stale); clothes.grubby: a grubby uniform (flag:clothes.grubby, AC3). Bubbles, 60 characters or fewer.
// Kind, never mean: the joke is on the clothes, not on you.
== clothes.remark
? flag:clothes.stale
- Yesterday's shirt. Brave. Wrong, but brave.   #funny
- I've seen that outfit before. Yesterday, mostly.   #funny
? flag:clothes.stale tier>=friend
- Change your shirt. I'm saying it because I like you.   #warm
== clothes.grubby
? flag:clothes.grubby
- You look like you lost a fight with a machine.   #funny
- Interesting look. Is the oil on purpose?   #funny
? flag:clothes.grubby tier>=friend
- Wardrobe. Now. I'll pretend I didn't see.   #warm

// ---- ZW1 (writer), patch 0.92.5 item 5: more lines for the chat card's opener (greet, near), so a tap doesn't repeat.
// Heard after a person's own lines are used up (FX13's no-repeat). {hi}, {nick} and {me} are the speaker's own words.
== greet
- Oh. It's you. Good. I was getting bored.
- {hi}. You're still here. Impressive.
- {hi}, {nick}. Don't tell me. You're lost.
- {hi}. I'd stand up, but I won't.
- Look who it is. My favourite interruption.
- {hi}. Say something interesting. No pressure.
- {hi}. You look awake. That makes one of us.
- {hi}. I was just thinking about nothing. You've ruined it.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {nick}. I'd say I missed you. I won't.
- {hi}. You again. I'm almost pleased.
? time:morning
- Morning. Allegedly.
? time:evening
- Evening. You survived the day. Congratulations.
== near
- Working. Don't look so surprised.
- {room}. Thrilling, as ever.
- I'll be done when I'm done. Hello, by the way.
- This is the exciting part. Watch closely. No, closer.
- I'm concentrating. You can tell by the face.
- Yes, I'm busy. No, you're not interrupting. Much.
- Some of us work. Some of us stand there. Hello.
- Don't touch that. Or do. See what happens.
